&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:calluna sans,calluna sans_embeddedfont,calluna sans_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;The M.J. Murdock Charitable Trust is a private, nonprofit foundation that has invested more than&amp;nbsp;$1.5&amp;nbsp;billion&amp;nbsp;in nonprofits serving the Pacific Northwest since 1975. For details, please visit our website&nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a class="Hyperlink SCXW123564366 BCX8" href="https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fmurdocktrust.org%2F&amp;amp;data=05%7C01%7C%7C494d7ee50c3d4603db4408daf97b7fd7%7Cf48c5e8fd82b48b89bb00b981e40a413%7C0%7C1%7C638096606065612725%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=ZviKg%2FClSYsCzUtdFhmS34xBGUv7odCJAA%2BKPm6xXw0%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0" rel="noreferrer noopener" style="-webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; text-decoration-line: none;" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;span style="color:rgb(80, 201, 181); font-family:calluna sans,calluna sans_embeddedfont,calluna sans_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;murdocktrust.org&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:calluna sans,calluna sans_embeddedfont,calluna sans_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:calluna sans,calluna sans_embeddedfont,calluna sans_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Please find the attached press release announcing Camp Spark&rsquo;s second-decade milestone and the launch of the 2026 season.&amp;nbsp;A digital media kit with supporting photos and video from Camp Spark is available &lt;a href="https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/kat11gow7eekm5v97agee/AIE4IKIB0dRiQSrQoXAvhEs/Winter%20Session?rlkey=ari8rkpddt8wllc5v6nn5d9n6&amp;amp;subfolder_nav_tracking=1&amp;amp;st=po3h38fw&amp;amp;dl=0"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HERE&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Starting tomorrow, 15 youth athletes who are blind or visually impaired will participate in adaptive winter recreation at Mt. Hood Kiwanis Camp through the Northwest Association for Blind Athletes (NWABA). Camp Spark is offered at no cost to families and has served 648 youth over the past decade, investing nearly $3 million to expand access to outdoor recreation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Should you like to cover the story in more depth, media are invited Saturday (2/28) from 10:00 a.m. &ndash; 1:00 p.m. to capture adaptive snow activities and interview leadership and campers. I will coordinate media onsite, and Programs Manager Matt Coelho will be available for interviews.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Please let me know if you&rsquo;re interested, and we&rsquo;d welcome your coverage in helping share this important program.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

