&lt;p&gt;&ldquo;Through the JA Stock Market Challenge, students gain handsâ'on experience with investing, risk management, and teamwork&mdash;skills that are essential for longâ'term financial success,&rdquo; said Natalie Vega O&rsquo;Neil, President &amp;amp; CEO of Junior Achievement of Washington. &ldquo;These students have demonstrated intense focus, adaptability, and confidence in a highâ'energy, realâ'world learning environment.&rdquo;&lt;br /&gt;
&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Winning teams have an opportunity to be chosen by the Future Bound Committee as one of the top teams in the nation and to compete in the national competition at Boston University June 7-11, 2026. Finalists will be announced by April 30, 2026. Washington had a team compete in the national contest in 2025 and placed third.&lt;br /&gt;
&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The JA Stock Market Challenge is part of Junior Achievement&rsquo;s broader mission to inspire and prepare young people to succeed in a global economy. Through experiential learning programs focused on financial capability, work readiness, and entrepreneurial mindset, JA helps students connect classroom learning to realâ'world opportunity.&lt;br /&gt;
&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;JA of Washington extends its gratitude to the educators, volunteers, and community partners who made the event possible, with special thanks to our title sponsor Amazon, with additional appreciation to Delta Air Lines, RSM, BlackRock, and PNC Bank for their generous support. Congratulations to all participating students for their commitment to learning, teamwork, and financial capability.&lt;br /&gt;
&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Junior Achievement of Washington&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Junior Achievement of Washington is the state&rsquo;s largest organization dedicated to preparing young people for economic success. Since 1953, JA of Washington has served more than two million students with handsâ'on learning experiences that teach financial capability, career readiness, and entrepreneurial mindset. Through partnerships with educators, volunteers, and the business community, JA helps students discover what&rsquo;s next for their futures. To learn more or get involved, visit Washington.ja.org.&lt;/p&gt;

